   $$extends an established practice to a component class it was not written for.$$, 31),
  ('7b03652e-309c-4566-9d82-864b4566c703', '0bb3878a-fb89-455d-a84c-bdb9a26b1643', '0e9200c0-a253-4489-9fa0-ac2b819c23bc', '4.5',
   $$Apply least-privilege and identity-lifecycle reasoning to a described access arrangement.$$,
   'high'::criticality, 'weekly'::task_frequency, '3_apply'::bloom_level,
   true, false,
   $$the identity lifecycle, least privilege, and privileged-access handling.$$,
   $$given a described access arrangement, determines whether the rights exceed what the role requires and identifies what would change.$$,
   $$reads access as a live risk surface rather than a settled configuration.$$, 32),
  ('3ed90a7c-6e14-48ef-9f5d-bfbfc09b72cc', '0bb3878a-fb89-455d-a84c-bdb9a26b1643', '0e9200c0-a253-4489-9fa0-ac2b819c23bc', '4.6',
   $$Analyze how access control assumptions break when a non-human actor holds credentials and acts.$$,
   'high'::criticality, 'occasional'::task_frequency, '4_analyze'::bloom_level,
   true, false,
   $$non-human identity, agent credentials, standing versus just-in-time authority, and the attribution problem.$$,
   $$given a described agent deployment, identifies which access-control assumption has stopped holding and explains why the conventional control does not address it.$$,
   $$recognizes when a control's underlying model, not its implementation, is what failed.$$, 33),
  ('18489a4a-9226-4552-9751-f6570c550186', '0bb3878a-fb89-455d-a84c-bdb9a26b1643', '0e9200c0-a253-4489-9fa0-ac2b819c23bc', '4.7',
   $$Explain supplier relationship controls and the security requirements placed on suppliers.$$,
   'high'::criticality, 'weekly'::task_frequency, '2_understand'::bloom_level,
   true, false,
   $$supplier controls, agreements, supply-chain reach, and delivery monitoring.$$,
   $$explains what security requirements a supplier relationship must carry and why monitoring continues past contract signature.$$,
   $$treats suppliers as part of the estate.$$, 34),
  ('f98701cd-c95f-42f0-a810-a7101d244b7f', '0bb3878a-fb89-455d-a84c-bdb9a26b1643', '0e9200c0-a253-4489-9fa0-ac2b819c23bc', '4.8',
   $$Analyze what supplier assurance can and cannot establish about a foundation-model provider.$$,
   'high'::criticality, 'occasional'::task_frequency, '4_analyze'::bloom_level,
   true, false,
   $$the foundation-model provider as a supplier, inspectability limits, attestation-based assurance, and concentration risk.$$,
   $$given a supplier assurance process applied to a model provider, identifies which questions the process cannot answer and why direct inspection is unavailable.$$,
   $$distinguishes assurance obtained from assurance assumed.$$, 35),
  ('0ed756d9-8d8d-496e-8da1-2a5d56b72373', '0bb3878a-fb89-455d-a84c-bdb9a26b1643', '0e9200c0-a253-4489-9fa0-ac2b819c23bc', '4.9',
   $$Explain the people controls theme - screening, terms, awareness, disciplinary process.$$,
   'medium'::criticality, 'weekly'::task_frequency, '2_understand'::bloom_level,
   true, false,
   $$the people theme and its control families across the employment lifecycle.$$,
   $$explains what each people control addresses and at which point in the employment relationship it applies.$$,
   $$recognizes that most security outcomes route through people.$$, 36),
  ('af5f4905-c653-423a-afd2-038d5070c9f8', '0bb3878a-fb89-455d-a84c-bdb9a26b1643', '0e9200c0-a253-4489-9fa0-ac2b819c23bc', '4.10',
   $$Apply awareness and acceptable-use reasoning to a described shadow AI situation.$$,
